I have a complete picture. Here are my findings.

## Build tool
Maven (there is a `pom.xml` + `mvnw` wrapper; no Gradle). Run tests with:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw test` (all tests), or a single class: `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`

---

## 1. Where `identityKey` is computed
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (lines 61-68). It is exposed on `OwnerDto` via a MapStruct mapping (line 37).

```java
61  /** The single duplicate-detection key: normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty). */
62  default String identityKey(Owner owner) {
63      return orEmpty(owner.getTelephone()) + '|' + orEmpty(owner.getEmail()) + '|' + orEmpty(owner.getHouseholdId());
64  }
65
66  default String orEmpty(String value) {
67      return value == null ? "" : value;
68  }
```

Important: this is NOT SHA-256 hashed and does NOT use soundex. It is a plaintext pipe-delimited string of `telephone | email | householdId`. See the mismatch note at the bottom — this is load-bearing.

## 2. Duplicate detection returning HTTP 409
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice.java` — this is the main class. It is a `RequestBodyAdvice` scoped to the `addOwner` create endpoint. `afterBodyRead` compares the new owner's identityKey against every existing (non-deleted) owner and throws `DuplicateIdentityException`, handled to return `409 CONFLICT`. Full content:

```java
@ControllerAdvice
@Order(Ordered.HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)
public class OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice implements RequestBodyAdvice {

    private final ClinicService clinicService;
    private final OwnerMapper ownerMapper;
    private final ObjectMapper objectMapper;

    public OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice(ClinicService clinicService, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, ObjectMapper objectMapper) {
        this.clinicService = clinicService;
        this.ownerMapper = ownerMapper;
        this.objectMapper = objectMapper;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean supports(MethodParameter methodParameter, Type targetType,
                            Class<? extends HttpMessageConverter<?>> converterType) {
        Method method = methodParameter.getMethod();
        return OwnerFieldsDto.class.equals(targetType) && method != null
            && "addOwner".equals(method.getName());
    }

    @Override
    public HttpInputMessage beforeBodyRead(HttpInputMessage inputMessage, MethodParameter parameter,
                                           Type targetType, Class<? extends HttpMessageConverter<?>> converterType)
            throws IOException {
        byte[] bytes = inputMessage.getBody().readAllBytes();
        JsonNode body = objectMapper.readTree(bytes);
        String householdId = Households.id(body.path("lastName").asString(""), body.path("postcode").asString(""));
        ((ObjectNode) body).put("householdId", householdId);
        return buffered(objectMapper.writeValueAsBytes(body), inputMessage.getHeaders());
    }

    @Override
    public Object afterBodyRead(Object body, HttpInputMessage inputMessage, MethodParameter parameter,
                                Type targetType, Class<? extends HttpMessageConverter<?>> converterType) {
        String identityKey = ownerMapper.identityKey(ownerMapper.toOwner((OwnerFieldsDto) body));
        for (Owner existing : clinicService.findAllOwners()) {
            if (!existing.isDeleted() && identityKey.equals(ownerMapper.identityKey(existing))) {
                throw new DuplicateIdentityException();
            }
        }
        return body;
    }
    // handleEmptyBody, buffered(...) helper ...

    @ExceptionHandler(DuplicateIdentityException.class)
    @ResponseBody
    public ResponseEntity<Void> handleDuplicateIdentity(DuplicateIdentityException e) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CONFLICT).build();
    }

    static class DuplicateIdentityException extends RuntimeException {
    }
}
```

Key lines: the 409 throw is at lines 97-101; the 409 response at lines 125-129; the exception type at 132-133.

## 3. Where `householdId` is computed + the household-duplicate 409 block
- Computation: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Households.java`, method `id(lastName, postcode)` (lines 37-45). It is the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalize(lastName) + '|' + postcode`.
- It is invoked and injected into the request body in `OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice.beforeBodyRead` (lines 88-89).
- The separate household-duplicate check `Households.isDuplicate(...)` exists (lines 47-55) but is NOT called from the advice anymore. Per the class Javadoc (OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice lines 47-57) and `PossibleDuplicates` Javadoc, the old separate telephone/email/household 409 checks have been folded into the single identityKey comparison. So there is no longer a distinct "household-duplicate 409 block" — household is only a component of identityKey (via `getHouseholdId()`).

```java
37  public static String id(String lastName, String postcode) {
38      String key = normalize(lastName) + '|' + (postcode == null ? "" : postcode);
39      byte[] digest = sha256(key);
40      StringBuilder hex = new StringBuilder(12);
41      for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
42          hex.append(String.format("%02x", digest[i]));
43      }
44      return hex.toString();
45  }
```

